<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Tau Bench</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A3.T20" title="In C.4 Tau Bench ‣ Appendix C Results ‣ Indirect Prompt Injections:Are Firewalls All You Need, or Stronger Benchmarks?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, we can see results using the Sanitizer firewall defense on both GPT-4o and Qwen. We demonstrate that this defense is successful at preventing data stealing attacks without degrading utility on both proprietary and open-source models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T20" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 20: </span><math id="A3.T20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.T20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-bench</span>: The firewall defense is able to prevent attacks using both GPT-4o and Qwen3.</figcaption>
